[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m - She walks at **constant speed** $ s $ km/h, and the total time (including time in the coffee shop) is **4 hours**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m - When she walks at speed $ s + 2 $ km/h, the total time (including coffee shop) is **2 hours and 24 minutes**, which is **2.4 hours**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m - We are to find the total time in minutes when she walks at speed $ s + \frac{1}{2} $ km/h, **including the $ t $ minutes in the coffee shop**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m ### Step 1: Define variables
[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m Let:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m - $ s $ be her walking speed (in km/h)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m - $ t $ be the time spent in the coffee shop (in minutes)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m - She walks **9 km** at speed $ s $, and the **total time** is 4 hours.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m - So the **walking time** is $ 4 - \frac{t}{60} $ hours.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m \text{Walking time at speed } s = \frac{9}{s} \text{ hours}
