[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m d = 2^a \times 3^b \times 5^c \times 7^d
[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m where $0 \leq a \leq 7$, $0 \leq b \leq 4$, $0 \leq c \leq 1$, and $0 \leq d \leq 1$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=39871)[0m But any number whose units digit is 1 cannot be divisible by 2 or 5 (because numbers ending in 1 can’t be even or divisible by 5). Thus, for such a number, the exponents of 2 and 5 in its factorization must be 0. That narrows things down.
